{
  "status": "implemented_seeded_defaults",
  "purpose": "Simple global Mapping output-template defaults, shared by logical_to_silver and dimensional_to_gold. Examples are synthetic.",
  "rules": [
    "The existing Mapping response envelope retains target identity, modeled_attribute_name and object_dependency_order. These templates describe only the inner transformation documents.",
    "Object fields include nullable source_objects, optional source_logical_entities, optional source_dimensional_entities, and nullable ordered steps. Logical Mapping uses physical inputs plus exposed Logical peer lookups. Dimensional Mapping uses Logical inputs plus exposed Dimensional peer lookups and sets source_objects to null.",
    "source_objects is a nullable list. Each entry is ordered tenant_code, system_code, connection_code, object_schema, object_name, alias. Use complete actual physical natural keys from eligible frozen evidence; no database IDs.",
    "Aliases are unique across every source list in one document. Self-join aliases may reference the same eligible source repeatedly.",
    "steps is a nullable ordered list of strings. It carries all Object transformation instructions: which Objects/tables to join, join types and exact column predicates, filters, grouping, deduplication, and additional processing when needed. Array order is execution order.",
    "Attribute source lists match the corresponding Object lists: source_attributes uses physical keys, source_logical_attributes uses Logical schema/entity/attribute keys, and source_dimensional_attributes uses Dimensional schema/entity/attribute keys. Each is optional and nullable. Dimensional fields are available only on the Dimensional route; physical fields remain null or absent there.",
    "transformation is required text containing the Attribute SQL expression or precise implementable generation rule, including needed cast/null/default/aggregation behavior. Use available Object aliases; put any self-join role distinction in transformation. There is no separate description field.",
    "The document_schema values below record the confirmed shapes and nullability. The existing output-template registry records field presence with is_required and explains nullability in descriptions; it has no separate nullable column. Runtime templates remain advisory.",
    "These approved definitions are the seeded global defaults for new Logical and Dimensional Mapping runs. Explicit custom template selections take precedence; existing saved mappings and frozen runs retain their original templates."
  ],
  "templates": [
    {
      "output_template_code": "mapping_object_default",
      "output_template_name": "Default Object Mapping",
      "output_template_description": "Describe physical inputs or modeled input/lookup sources and ordered Entity transformation steps.",
      "output_template_target_type": "mapping_object",
      "fields": [
        {
          "output_template_field_name": "source_objects",
          "output_template_field_description": "Nullable list of source Objects. Each entry has tenant_code, system_code, connection_code, object_schema, object_name, alias, in that order. The field is present and may be JSON null. Use only for Logical Mapping; set null for Dimensional Mapping.",
          "output_template_field_data_type": "array",
          "output_template_field_array_item_type": "object",
          "output_template_field_is_required": true,
          "output_template_field_order": 1,
          "output_template_field_example": [
            {
              "tenant_code": "NWA",
              "system_code": "GDS",
              "connection_code": "lakehouse",
              "object_schema": "bronze_crm",
              "object_name": "customer",
              "alias": "c"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "output_template_field_name": "source_logical_entities",
          "output_template_field_description": "Optional nullable Logical Entity sources for Dimensional input or Logical foreign-key lookups. Each entry has logical_entity_schema_name, logical_entity_name, alias. Use only frozen eligible source evidence.",
          "output_template_field_data_type": "array",
          "output_template_field_array_item_type": "object",
          "output_template_field_is_required": false,
          "output_template_field_order": 2,
          "output_template_field_example": [
